# Credentials — never commit these
# .env, .env.local, ".env copy.example" — any variant may hold real secrets;
# the committed template (.env.example) is re-included below.
.env*
!.env.example
Neo4j-*.txt

# Local Claude settings (machine-local paths / personal permission rules)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Node (web/)
node_modules/

# ADK local runtime state (agents/ — session DBs the api_server writes)
.adk/

# Test / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Sample / local data — may contain sensitive source data
drydocs/data/
# Staging / extract output (real data — keep local, never commit)
stg_out/
/stg_*/

# SDLC-Docs — Fidelity-internal source corpus: keep LOCAL for reference, never commit/publish.
# Internal-Confidential per PUBLISH-BOUNDARY.md (real org name "Fidelity/FMR", internal fmr.com
# URLs, internal tool/standard code names). Ignore the WHOLE corpus (docx/doc/pdf/xls/txt/json,
# any type) and keep only the clean design artifacts SDLC-Docs/extracted/*.md tracked.
/SDLC-Docs/*
!/SDLC-Docs/extracted/
/SDLC-Docs/extracted/*
!/SDLC-Docs/extracted/*.md

# Local doc-extraction helper scripts (temporary; generated the SDLC-Docs corpus)
/.tmp_*

# Oracle Kerberos connection — the FILLED config holds a real SID/hosts/alias.
# Only the .sample.txt is committed.
libs/oracle_kerberos/oracle_kerberos_connection.txt

# Local real-data working area (Internal-Confidential): consolidated
# troubleshooting notes, screenshots with live values, filled configs.
# Never committed; travels to the company side by hand, not by git.
/internal-local/

# Raw screenshots/images dropped in the REPO ROOT during troubleshooting/porting —
# they routinely contain live SIDs, hostnames, EPV objects, ADFS client IDs.
# Blanket rule: no root-level images are ever committed (verified: none tracked).
# Committed images live in purposeful homes (drydocs-icons/, docs/). Move drops
# into internal-local/ when done; this is the safety net.
/*.png
/*.webp
/*.svg
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Books / reports dropped in the REPO ROOT (e.g. Essential-GraphRAG.pdf — publicly
# available Manning/Neo4j ebook, cite by URL; annual-report inputs). Publisher PDFs
# are never committed (copyright + repo size); the registration lives in
# reference/research/README.md. Tracked PDFs live in purposeful homes (UI-WIP/).
/*.pdf

# Vendor PDF posters/manuals — copyrighted BMC (and other vendor) binaries kept
# as LOCAL reference only. This repo is sometimes published; the *.md files in
# external/orchestration/ are our own summaries and are publishable, the raw
# vendor PDFs are not. Facts from the poster are transcribed in the controlm-db
# skill (references/er-model.md).
external/orchestration/**/*.pdf

# Design-doc PDFs (Epic L / L4) — BUILD-ON-DEMAND from the .md via scripts/doc_to_pdf.py.
# The .md is the source of truth and the .html/.print.html renders are committed; the PDF is a
# regenerable binary (not byte-identical run-to-run — trailer /ID varies), so it is not tracked.
# Regenerate before printing for the pen/paper loop.
docs/design/*.pdf

# Paper-HITL scans (Epic L / L6) — raw scanned/photographed annotated printouts. Internal
# by default (see docs/design/feedback/scans/README.md + config/classification.yaml
# excluded_paths): never published unless a human deliberately reclassifies. Keep the
# README (the classification note) tracked; the raw scans are not.
docs/design/feedback/scans/*
!docs/design/feedback/scans/README.md

# Editor workspace settings (machine-local)
/.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
